item: u4-l3-choice-symptoms

card c07
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: A big dose, quickly
figure: big-fast-dose
figure_at: 1

body:
    About 1 sievert, or 1000 millisieverts, in a short time is the threshold for [[acute-radiation-syndrome|acute radiation syndrome]]. Within hours it can cause symptoms such as nausea and vomiting. High doses can also cause skin redness, hair loss and burns.

card c08
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: Small doses, spread out
figure: small-spread-dose
figure_at: 1

body:
    Low levels of radiation do not cause immediate health effects. They can add a small increase in the risk of cancer over a lifetime. If a dose is low or spread over a long time, the risk is lower, because repair is more likely.

