card c12
kind: teach
type: explain
tier: deeper
scored: 0
title: Go deeper: a one-time 100
figure: small-spread-dose
figure_at: 1

body:
    About 99 in 100 people given a one-time dose of 100 millisieverts would not get cancer as a result. At that dose, extra cancers caused by radiation would be extremely difficult to identify.
